From: Steam-Link-PS5
Subject: video: don't freeze on a stalled partial frame either (patch 0019)

Follow-up to 0018 after the user reported the stutter was no better. Per-frame
instrumentation (present cadence + arrival-gap histograms) showed two things 0018
had not: constant present judder from arrival jitter, and - the big one - periodic
200-640 ms hitches whose arrival gaps lined up exactly with "Partial frames stalled
for 150 ms, request keyframe" followed by "33/35/36 partial frames was cleared".

CheckPartialOverflow was the other hard-freeze path 0018 left in place: when one
frame never received all its fragments (a lost packet), it requested a keyframe and
set waitingKeyFrame, so every following frame was dropped until a full IDR arrived -
the keyframe round-trip being the 200-640 ms hitch, firing ~9 times in 40 s.

Make it soft, matching 0018's sequence-gap handling: drop the stuck partials
(DiscardPending) so assembly advances to the next frame, reset the assembly flags,
ask for a keyframe once (coalesced via keyframeAskedAt) to heal cleanly, and KEEP
DECODING. A missing-fragment frame becomes a brief artifact the next keyframe wipes,
not a multi-hundred-ms freeze. The decoder reset path (SubmitFrame ReportLost ->
ApplyDecoderReset) remains the backstop for a genuinely undecodable frame.

This kills the big hitches. The remaining constant judder is the absence of a
presentation jitter buffer (present-latest-every-vblank turns arrival jitter into
repeats/skips); that is a separate, larger change with a latency tradeoff, tracked
separately.

